response:
{The color gamut is defined as the range of colors that a particular device can produce or record.}
{It is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram.}
{The color gamut of a monitor is shown in a triangular area enclosed by the color coordinates of the monitor's red, green, and blue colors.}
{A chromaticity diagram with different color gamuts is shown in Figure 1.}
{The most commonly known color gamut might be “NTSC” (established in 1953 by the US FCC), however, it is not a standard color gamut.}
